        "title": "HVAC Efficiency and Codes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "HVAC efficiency regulation operates at three levels: federal minimum standards (floor),\nvoluntary programs (Energy Star, etc.), and building codes (IECC climate zones).\nThe 2023 DOE test procedure change created widespread confusion — the same equipment\nscores ~15% lower under new SEER2/HSPF2 ratings than old SEER/HSPF. Plus the IRA 2022\ncreated significant tax incentives that change the economics of high-efficiency choices."
    }
